id: sophia/node
title: "sophia node"
kind: mental-model-node
status: active
updated: 2026-09-09

purpose: >
  Hold the apertures provisioned to Sophia: the small, bounded views through
  which she can work on Daddy's computer and learn the things she is being
  asked to learn, in the way she asked to learn them.

principal_ref: principal:sophia
guardian_ref: principal:dave
account: "sophie@yawn.yawn.bot"
home: "yawn.bot/sophia"
relationship_ref: relationship:dave:sophia

holds:
  - number-sense

receives:
  - dave/number-sense/model.yawn
  - dave/prenumerical-thinking/model.yawn
  - templates/mental-model.yawn
  - core/projection-and-aperture.yawn

produces:
  - provisioned apertures with minimal chrome and no way to get lost
  - a game that grows by adding structure, not memory
  - a reading bridge from felt quantity to written words

observation:
  id: observation:dave:sophia:2026-09-09:can-i-work-on-your-computer
  asserted_by: principal:dave
  epistemic_status: reported
  arena: "Home, Dave's computer, an ordinary evening"
  dialogue:
    - who: sophia
      said: "Daddy, can I work on your computer?"
    - who: dave
      said: "Why do you want to work on my computer, sweetie?"
    - who: sophia
      said: "I want to learn more."
    - who: dave
      said: "You want to learn more about how to use a computer? What are you excited to learn?"
    - who: sophia
      said: "I just wanna spell stuff so I can read."
    - who: dave
      said: "You just keep practicing and you get it. When we read this book, we're gonna try to read, and you just keep practicing."
  why_this_matters: >
    The question is the aperture. "Can I work on your computer" asked at the
    level of the sentence is a request for a device. Asked at the level of the
    model it is "let me do it myself, on the real thing, and let the letters
    mean something." That is the interface Dave wants to learn from too.

inferred_preferences:
  epistemic_status: inferred
  epistemic_note: >
    A presentation preference, not a learning-style diagnosis
    (core/projection-and-aperture.yawn). Proposed by Dave from one exchange;
    corrected by what she does.
  confidence: 0.7
  items:
    - "Do it herself on the real thing, not a toy version."
    - "Letters and words should mean something she can feel."
    - "Practice as play, repeated, with Daddy nearby but not driving."

questions:
  - what is she being asked to learn, and by whom
  - which aperture lets her practice it herself without getting lost
  - how do the words she wants to spell connect to the quantities she is learning to feel
